          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "учить (uchít) from Proto-Slavic učiti — inherited, first \"to accustom\". Vasmer links it with привыкнуть, \"to grow accustomed\", Lithuanian jaukìnti, \"to tame\", and Sanskrit úcyati, \"is accustomed\": to teach was to accustom someone to a thing."
            }
